    affiliation: Istinye University, Department of Software Engineering
contact:
  - given-names: Ege
    family-names: Karaurgan
    affiliation: Istinye University, Department of Software Engineering
abstract: >-
  A computer-vision pipeline that estimates elevator cabin
  occupancy from a single CCTV frame and decides whether
  incoming hall calls should be served or bypassed. The
  system combines a YOLOv8 object detector (trained on a
  unified four-class dataset of persons, strollers, luggage,
  and boxes) with a class-based footprint area estimator
  grounded in TS EN 81-20 / ISO 8100 elevator capacity
  standards. A power-consumption model after Tukia et al.
  (2018) quantifies the energy savings of the proposed
  control policy relative to a weight-only baseline.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - YOLOv8
  - object detection
  - elevator control
  - energy efficiency
  - smart buildings
  - occupancy estimation
